WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.520
At 23 years old, to be given a quarter of a million dollars to go build a company and to say no to that

00:05.520 --> 00:08.620
is something people have told me, we thought you were insane.

00:08.920 --> 00:13.460
This is Zain, and in the past few years he's been studying law, acting in an HBO show,

00:13.720 --> 00:19.360
working for a little company called Monzo, and turned down £250,000 in investor cash.

00:19.520 --> 00:22.040
All because he realised he was working on the wrong thing.

00:22.280 --> 00:24.880
As a British Pakistani, you're in between two identities.

00:24.880 --> 00:29.720
You are cheering for England in the World Cup, but then at home you're eating biryani, right?

00:29.720 --> 00:33.940
So you're living between these two identities and you're in a search for those shared spaces.

00:34.180 --> 00:40.000
So Zain and his best friend Habeeb tried to find a way to help people in their community feel closer to both of their homes.

00:40.520 --> 00:47.380
Habeeb told me a story once about how in his local community in Halifax, people used to pool funds together to support each other when they needed it.

00:47.420 --> 00:49.900
And then we went searching for something like that for South Asia.

00:50.340 --> 00:53.360
We couldn't find one. So I gave Habeeb the ring and said, let's build it.

00:53.500 --> 00:58.940
So together they built Saath, a community-led fund that kickstarts locally-led projects across South Asia.

00:58.940 --> 01:01.860
We'd spent five months tinkering with different tools.

01:02.060 --> 01:05.800
It was about like a day or two away from us wanting to launch.

01:06.380 --> 01:07.880
And we wanted to change a button.

01:08.200 --> 01:08.880
We couldn't change the button.

01:09.020 --> 01:11.800
We wanted to change how much money people can contribute when they sign up.

01:11.960 --> 01:12.760
We couldn't figure that out.

01:12.860 --> 01:16.100
And it was frustrating because we had such a big vision for what we wanted to do.

01:16.200 --> 01:20.000
So we're like, Habeeb, we should, let's try this AI app builder tool called Lovable.

01:20.220 --> 01:20.900
I open it up.

01:20.980 --> 01:22.300
I just completely ramble.

01:22.420 --> 01:23.120
I'm like, this is what I want.

01:23.180 --> 01:23.840
These are the colors.

01:24.080 --> 01:25.320
This is the platform.

01:25.320 --> 01:31.760
And then everything I had over here in my head was exactly what popped up on the screen.

01:31.920 --> 01:34.580
And 24 hours later, we were live and running.

01:34.900 --> 01:36.500
And with that, Saath was built,

01:36.680 --> 01:40.580
an online fund that lets the people who donate the money actually choose where it goes.

01:40.720 --> 01:45.420
From a girls' football club in Nepal to a craftswoman academy which turns old clothes into new bags,

01:45.680 --> 01:47.420
Zain isn't just making one-off payments.

01:47.780 --> 01:52.340
He's helping to fund businesses across South Asia that will sustain themselves for years to come.

01:52.540 --> 01:56.040
I remember we saw the football academy live,

01:56.620 --> 01:59.480
people running around a pitch with a shirt which had a logo on it.

01:59.600 --> 02:01.660
And we're like, we're just two kids behind a laptop

02:01.660 --> 02:03.300
and now there's a football academy that exists

02:03.300 --> 02:04.600
in a place we've never stepped foot in.

02:04.720 --> 02:05.640
That was mind-blowing.

02:06.000 --> 02:07.440
You know, if you have five pounds alone,

02:07.560 --> 02:08.500
that can do a tiny bit,

02:08.580 --> 02:10.980
but if you put thousands of people together,

02:11.300 --> 02:12.560
not even just putting in money,

02:12.660 --> 02:14.700
but also their resources, their network and everything,

02:14.920 --> 02:17.460
you can bring really ambitious ideas to life.
